FROZEN SINCE YOUR PACKET WAS WRITTEN — u3 owns these and you consume them verbatim; they are contract, not proposal:

  pub struct FileRefOutcome { pub attached: usize, pub unattached: Vec<String> }
  pub async fn replace_file_refs(pool, blob: &BlobRef, parser_version: &str, refs: &[DdocFileRef])
      -> Result<FileRefOutcome, StoreError>;

Semantics, ruled: `attached` counts post-replacement rows for refs whose source address resolved in the exact blob/parser scope, with duplicate identical input edges collapsing under the UNIQUE key. `unattached` lists each unresolved source address in INPUT ORDER, including repeats. A source miss is NEVER a StoreError — StoreError means the database refused. Resolution is exact scope + address + kind='row', never another blob/parser and never a code element.

YOUR OBLIGATION: surface `unattached` as row findings rather than discarding it. An edge we could not attach is exactly the kind of thing that must stay queryable instead of becoming invisible — the same rule as EmbedBasis::Fallback. Discarding it silently is a review-blocking defect.
